<title>FRANCE: ADP - Paris Jan-Feb 97 import traffic up 3.8pct.</title>
<headline>ADP - Paris Jan-Feb 97 import traffic up 3.8pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-February 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 83,417 tonnes, an increase of 3.8 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The Paris airports January-February 1997 import traffic, by region, with percentage change against the same period 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>			    Tonnes   Pct change on</p>
<p>					 Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p> Domestic		  4,739   down  7.5pct</p>
<p> European Union	 10,169   up   14.5</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	   2,036   up   22.8</p>
<p> North Africa	    1,862   down 25.9</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa    9,395   down  1.9</p>
<p> North America	  26,999   down  5.1</p>
<p> French territories    1,892   up   19.0</p>
<p> Latin America	   3,150   down  3.0</p>
<p> Middle East	     3,896   up    5.2</p>
<p> Far East		 19,278   up   21.7</p>
<p> Total		    83,416   up    3.8</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
